[Chapter "Two Knights Attack"]
[Line "6.d4 and the d-pawn"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defense: Two Knights Attack, Mindeno Variation, Exchange Line"]

{White develops both knights first. Black pins the f3 knight and gives the bishop for it.} 1. e4 c6 {The Caro-Kann.} 2. Nc3 d5 {Challenge e4 anyway.} 3. Nf3 {The Two Knights Attack.} 3... Bg4 {Pin the knight and develop the bishop before ...e6.} 4. h3 Bxf3 {Give the bishop for the knight. White gets the bishop pair, Black gets a solid, easy position.} 5. Qxf3 e6 {Support d5 and open the f8 bishop.} 6. d4 Nf6 {Develop and add pressure on e4.} 7. Bd3 dxe4 {Release the centre.} 8. Nxe4 Qxd4 {White has offered the d-pawn, and Black can take it.} 9. c3 Qd8 {Bring the queen home. Black is a pawn up; White has the bishop pair and faster development in return.} *
